Article 2 The State shall implement a production license system for enterprises producing the following important industrial products:
(1) processed food directly related to human health, such as dairy products, meat products, beverages, rice, flour, edible oil, and alcoholic beverages;
(2) products that may endanger personal or property safety, such as electric blankets, pressure cookers, and gas water heaters;
(3) products related to financial security and communication quality safety, such as tax-controlled cash registers, anti-counterfeit bill detectors, satellite television broadcast ground receiving equipment, and wireless broadcast television transmission equipment;
(4) products ensuring labor safety, such as safety nets, safety helmets, and building fasteners;
(5) products affecting production safety and public safety, such as power transmission towers, bridge bearings, railway industrial products, hydraulic metal structures, dangerous chemicals and their packaging materials and containers;
(6) other products that laws or administrative regulations require to be subject to production license management in accordance with these Regulations.

Article 9 An enterprise shall meet the following conditions to obtain a production license:
(1) having a business license;
(2) having professional technical personnel suitable for the products it produces;
(3) having production conditions and inspection and quarantine means suitable for the products it produces;
(4) having technical documents and process documents suitable for the products it produces;
(5) having a sound and effective quality management system and responsibility system;
(6) the products conforming to relevant national standards, industry standards, and the requirements for ensuring human health and personal and property safety;
(7) conforming to the provisions of national industrial policies, and there being no situations of backward processes, high energy consumption, environmental pollution, or waste of resources that are explicitly eliminated or prohibited from investment and construction by the State.
If laws or administrative regulations have other provisions, those provisions shall also be complied with.

Article 37 The competent departments of industrial product production licenses at or above the county level shall, based on obtained evidence of suspected illegality or reports, investigate and handle acts suspected of violating these Regulations and may exercise the following powers:
(1) to investigate and learn about information concerning suspected activities violating these Regulations from the legal representatives, principal responsible persons, and other relevant personnel of units that produce, sell, or use products included in the Catalog in business activities, and from inspection institutions;
(2) to consult and copy relevant contracts, invoices, account books, and other relevant materials of units that produce, sell, or use products included in the Catalog in business activities, and of inspection institutions;
(3) to seal up or seize products included in the Catalog that are produced, sold, or used in business activities in violation of these Regulations, as evidenced.

Article 60 If the competent departments of industrial product production licenses or their staff members violate the provisions of these Regulations in any of the following circumstances, their superior administrative organs or supervisory organs shall order them to make corrections; if the circumstances are serious, administrative sanctions shall be imposed on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible personnel according to law:
(1) failing to accept an application that meets the conditions prescribed in these Regulations;
(2) failing to publicly display materials that shall be publicly displayed according to law at the office premises;
(3) failing to perform the statutory obligation to inform the applicant or interested parties during the process of acceptance, examination, and decision;
(4) failing to inform the applicant at once of all the contents that need to be supplemented when the application materials submitted by the applicant are incomplete or do not conform to the statutory form;
(5) failing to state the reasons for not accepting an application or not granting a license according to law;
(6) failing to hold a hearing that shall be held in accordance with these Regulations and the Administrative License Law of the People's Republic of China.

Article 62 If a competent department of industrial product production licenses is in any of the following circumstances, its superior administrative organ, supervisory organ, or relevant organ shall order it to make corrections and handle the matter according to law; administrative sanctions of demotion or removal from office shall be imposed on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible personnel according to law; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) granting a license to an applicant who does not meet the conditions prescribed in these Regulations, or making a decision to grant a license beyond its statutory authority;
(2) refusing to grant a license to an applicant who meets the conditions prescribed in these Regulations, or failing to make a decision on granting a license within the statutory time limit;
(3) discovering that a person produces products included in the Catalog without applying for and obtaining a production license in accordance with these Regulations, and failing to investigate and handle the matter promptly according to law;
(4) discovering that the inspection report or inspection conclusion of an inspection institution is seriously false, and failing to investigate and handle the matter promptly according to law;
(5) illegally charging fees in violation of laws, administrative regulations, or these Regulations.
